   "source": [
    "# Caustic module usage\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook shows the real workflow behind the caustic helper module:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. acquire a raw beam image from Shadow,\n",
    "2. turn that image ticket into a `Histogram2DAnalyzer`,\n",
    "3. compute moment-based estimates,\n",
    "4. run the Gaussian fit explicitly,\n",
    "5. use the fitted widths in a caustic scan.\n",
    "\n",
    "The key point is: the object returned by `save_image()` is not itself a fitted analyzer. It is a data container. The fit lives in `Histogram2DAnalyzer`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "2c72df93",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
