   "source": [
    "## Practical rule\n",
    "\n",
    "- `save_image()` and `Image` only give the raw histogram ticket.\n",
    "- `Histogram2DAnalyzer` is where the beam fitting happens.\n",
    "- `caustic.py` is only the scan-and-fit helper around those measurements.\n",
    "- The fitted caustic result is used to estimate the focus minimum; the image-level fit still drives the width and uncertainty values."
   ]
